It depends on your dexterity, I believe.  If your dex is too low, you
run into the door, otherwise you are simply told that the door is
closed.

With that in mind, I don't think that this changes gameplay at all, if
you leave in the DEX check before applying the auto-open rules.  And
having the autokick always on (ie. not an option) is a wondeful way to
keep players on their toes.  If you're going to save the player some
effort, there's good logic to making mistakes costly.
